/* Localized display names for the Input Source picker. Without this
   file, macOS falls back to showing the raw TISInputSourceID string
   instead of a human-readable name — confirmed by comparing against
   macSKK's own Contents/Resources/InfoPlist.strings, which follows
   the same pattern (CFBundleName + one entry per TISInputSourceID).

   "ひらがな (Nagi)", not the plain "ひらがな" M1 shipped with: other
   Japanese IMEs (Google 日本語入力, macSKK, Kotoeri) all register a mode
   named exactly "ひらがな" too, so a bare "ひらがな" is indistinguishable
   from theirs in the Input Sources list — see issue #6, item 1. */
"CFBundleName" = "Nagi";
"com.nvleo.inputmethod.nagi.Hiragana" = "ひらがな (Nagi)";
